===CCXR Trevita===
The CCXR '''''Trevita''''' is a limited edition of the Koenigsegg CCXR featuring a diamond weave carbon fibre finish. ''Trevita'' is an abbreviation in Swedish and translates into "three whites".<ref>{{cite web | last = Press Release | first = Koenigsegg | title = The Koenigsegg Trevita – The Shimmering Diamond | date = 9 September 2009 | url = http://www.koenigsegg.com/news.php | access-date = 25 June 2013 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20110205051948/http://koenigsegg.com/news.php | archive-date = 5 February 2011 | url-status = dead }}</ref> The Koenigsegg Proprietary Diamond Weave, fully developed by Koenigsegg, is a new and unique method to manufacture the carbon fibre used for the CCXR Trevita. By utilising this new and unique method, Koenigsegg managed to coat the fibres with a diamond finish. The fibre treatment is conducted carefully in small quantities, prior to further processing the pre-production material.<ref name="thewashingtontimes">{{cite web|url=http://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2009/sep/18/koenigseggs-trevita-is-unique/|title=Koenigsegg's Trevita is unique|publisher=[[The Washington Times]]|date=18 September 2009|access-date=12 October 2009|archive-date=15 October 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121015001902/http://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2009/sep/18/koenigseggs-trevita-is-unique/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Initially, three CCXR Trevitas were planned to be produced, however, because of the complexity to make the special diamond weave carbon-fibre, only 2 were ever made, making it one of the rarest vehicles manufactured by Koenigsegg. Both cars featured the Koenigsegg Shimmering Diamond Weave bodywork, twin-deck carbon fibre rear wing, [[inconel]] exhaust system, carbon ceramic brakes with ABS, airbags, F1 paddle-shift gearbox, chrono instrument cluster, infotainment system, tire monitoring system and a hydraulic lifting system.<ref name="GTSpirit">{{cite web |url=http://www.gtspirit.com/2009/09/10/koenigsegg-trevita/ |title=Koenigsegg Trevita |work=GTspirit.com |date=10 September 2009 |access-date=12 October 2009 |archive-date=31 October 2009 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091031231537/http://www.gtspirit.com/2009/09/10/koenigsegg-trevita/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The Trevita is also one of the most expensive sports cars, costing [[United States Dollar|US$]]4.8 million.<ref>{{cite web
