==Awards and recognition==
* 2009 Best Performing Green Exotic, ''[[duPont Registry]]''<ref name="DuPontAward">{{cite web |url=http://www.autoblog.com/2008/10/09/dupont-registrys-11-best-of-cars-set-horsepower-price-record/ |title=duPont Registry's 11 "Best of" cars set horsepower, price records |access-date=20 March 2008 |last=Ramsey |first=Jonathon |date=9 October 2008 |work=[[Autoblog.com|Autoblog]] |publisher=[[Weblogs, Inc.]] |archive-date=12 October 2008 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081012062211/http://www.autoblog.com/2008/10/09/dupont-registrys-11-best-of-cars-set-horsepower-price-record/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
* One of the 10 Most Beautiful Cars by ''[[Forbes]]'' magazine

In 2007, the CCX was the fastest car to complete ''[[Top Gear (2002 TV series)|Top Gear]]''{{'}}s [[Power Laps|Power Lap]] with a time of 1:17.6 (until it was beaten by the [[Ascari A10]] with a time of 1:17.3).<ref name="powerlaps">{{cite web|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/topgear/show/powerlaps.shtml|title=Top Gear – Power Laps|publisher=BBC|access-date=15 October 2007|archive-date=21 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210221072249/http://www.bbc.co.uk/topgear/show/powerlaps.shtml|url-status=dead}}</ref>  The car originally lapped the circuit in 1:20.4, but was then fitted with an optional rear [[spoiler (automotive)|wing]] to provide [[downforce]] after [[The Stig]] spun it off the track at 130&nbsp;mph due to a power steering failure. The Stig purportedly recommended this modification, predicting that the car would then be the fastest ever round ''Top Gear''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s track<ref name="topgear81">{{cite episode|series=[[Top Gear (2002 TV series format)|Top Gear]]|series-no=8|number=1|airdate=7 May 2006}} – Jeremy Clarkson: "After the accident, Stig said he reckons this car would be 4 seconds faster than it was if it had a big wing on the back."</ref> but Koenigsegg later stated that the improvement was due to adjustments to the chassis and suspension settings and not the addition of the rear spoiler. Despite this, the Stig's spoiler-idea remained the credited reason for the improved lap time.<ref name="bilsportresponse">{{cite web|author=Svensson, Gunnar|url=http://www.bilsport.se/news.php?id=36110|title=Koenigsegg får Top Gear-vinge|language=sv|publisher=[[Bilsport]]|date=5 June 2006|access-date=12 March 2007|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070406145120/http://www.bilsport.se/news.php?id=36110|archive-date=6 April 2007}}</ref> The name of the car on the lap board is "Koeniggggsenisseggsegnignigsegigiseg CCX2 with the Top Gear wing", reportedly because none of the ''Top Gear'' presenters knew how to spell Koenigsegg, and also poking fun at the long and hard pronunciation of the manufacturer's name.

